48
00:03:58.512 --> 00:04:05.122
Scene understanding combines objects, layout,
and contextual relationships.

49
00:04:05.122 --> 00:04:12.635
Consider this worked case: A street scene is
interpreted by recognizing a pedestrian, a

50
00:04:12.635 --> 00:04:19.611
road, and a building, then assigning semantic
relationships such as 'standing on' and

51
00:04:19.611 --> 00:04:20.684
'adjacent to'.

52
00:04:20.684 --> 00:04:27.872
State the benefit, the cost, and the condition
under which the tradeoff is acceptable.

53
00:04:27.872 --> 00:04:34.950
Making the tradeoff visible prevents a local
improvement from hiding a larger cost.

54
00:04:35.066 --> 00:04:42.119
Stress-test the reasoning around Image
Representation & Conversion with an edge case

55
00:04:42.119 --> 00:04:46.234
and identify which assumption controls the
outcome.

56
00:04:46.234 --> 00:04:51.859
Computer vision pipelines represent images as
numeric arrays.

57
00:04:51.859 --> 00:05:00.489
Consider this worked case: A color image is
converted from RGB to HSV space to isolate

58
00:05:00.489 --> 00:05:05.344
